p2-windows/W7 — page:notifications/Channels — native WinUI 3 ChannelsPage at web parity
=======================================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/notifications/pages/ChannelsPage.tsx
Web route  : /notifications/channels  (nav name "Channels")
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ChannelsPage/{ChannelsPage.cs,
             ChannelsPage.Model.cs, ChannelsPage.ViewModel.cs}
             (real in-repo path; the generated prompt's apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Notifications
              path does not exist — the Windows app is TeslaSync.App with C#-markup feature-views,
              not XAML-per-page, and the platform string catalog lives at apps/windows/Strings/*.resw.
              This mirrors every prior W7 page in apps/parity/windows-ledger.json.)

Shape of the parity unit
------------------------
The web page is a thin shell: a <PageContainer title subtitle copyLink> hosting <NotificationChannelsView />.
It declares NO data sources, NO named panels, NO charts, NO maps and NO data states of its own — the manifest
record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:notifications/Channels) lists requiredCount=2, both strings.
The hosted NotificationChannelsView is a separate, already-covered parity unit that owns its own four data
states; this page owns only the titled, copy-link page-container chrome.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011)
--------------------------------------------------------------
- ChannelsPage : UserControl  — mounts the native PageContainer shared surface (the parity port of the web
  PageContainer, apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/PageContainer.cs) with CopyLink=true and
  PageContent = new NotificationChannelsView(...), reproducing the web tree 1:1.
- ChannelsPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — the UI-thread-free state holder. With no data source it
  resolves the page chrome (title + subtitle) through the injected ILocalizer and projects ChannelsPageDisplay;
  LoadAsync/RefreshAsync exist for the page-lifecycle contract (re-resolve on locale change). No I/O in the view.
- ChannelsPageRegistration — RouteName="NotificationsChannels" (matches RouteTable.cs L136
  Page("NotificationsChannels","notifications/channels",RouteGroup.Notifications,"Channels")), Slug="ChannelsPage",
  Title/Subtitle keyed through ILocalizer with the web key names + the web inline-default English copy.
- EmptyNotificationChannelsSource — the no-backend feed the parameterless (shell-registered) page hosts the
  channels view against, mirroring the other W7 pages' Empty*Source defaults.
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("NotificationsChannels", () => new FeatureViews.Notifications.ChannelsPage()).

i18n note (R3/ADR-014)
----------------------
notifications.channels.title / .subtitle are NOT catalog entries in either the web i18n source
(web/src/i18n/en.json) or the generated platform catalog (apps/windows/Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw) —
the web resolves them as inline t(key, default) fallbacks. The native surface resolves them the same way:
keyed ILocalizer.GetString(key, <same English default>) flowing through ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization
(resw lookup -> English fallback). Zero hardcoded literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched (it is
machine-generated from web i18n by apps/shared/i18n/generators/gen-i18n.ts — hand-editing would strand drift).

